    "minimal_option": "Additive versioned non-served epistemic/primary-intent diagnostic, preserving role UNKNOWN and all old hashes. Separate scientifically supported primary intent from unresolved ancillary accounting. Do not claim this grants old-v1 admission or removes old-v1 CATALOG_GAP.",
    "amendment_boundary": "Accepting nonblocking ancillary UNKNOWN into the initial admissible set requires an explicit versioned curation/admission-gate decision; it does not itself require changing the catalogue enum. Allowing an executable READY with partial exposure additionally requires an explicit FirstPlan version/semantics amendment. Neither binding nor READY is owned by the present spike."
  },
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "claim": "Catalogue publication already admits incomplete exposure vectors: reviewed + at least one resolved PRIMARY suffices; UNKNOWN blocks use of that zone as PRIMARY and marks vector incomplete, rather than invalidating other primary zones.",
      "refs": [
        "data/sci/exercise_catalogue.schema.json:595-645",
        "data/sci/exercise_catalogue.schema.json:803-830",
        "scripts/validate_sci_catalogue.py:430-449"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "claim": "Scientific historical exposure already supports partial accounting: known roles accumulate resolved_credit, UNKNOWN increments unknown_sets; affected zone MINIMUM. Unknown identity makes every zone MINIMUM. Execution uncertainty remains a separate exact_evidence guard. These are non-served read-only modules.",
      "refs": [
        "app/services/sci_exposure.py:18-26",
        "app/services/sci_exposure.py:136-185",
        "tests/test_sci_exposure.py:188-228",
        "tests/test_sci_exposure.py:259-286"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "claim": "The exact-exposure INITIAL admission blocker is narrower and stricter: curation1.0.0 refuses any eligible candidate with any UNKNOWN; resolver admits only ELIGIBLE reviewed dispositions. All five vertical candidates remain held, so old curation CATALOG_GAP is correct under its own contract.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_initial_policy/curation.py:180-181",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/curation.py:212-273",
        "tests/test_science_candidate_curation.py:129-135"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "claim": "Initial producer planning already selects by primary zone + pattern, independent of ancillary-role completeness, but its non-executable diagnostics null credit/mark UNKNOWN for each unknown exposure and append CATALOG_GAP. This diagnostic choice is not catalogue-wide biology and is independent of the later curation overlay, which the producer does not import.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_initial_policy/planning.py:61-115",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/planning.py:131-200",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/producer.py:101-123"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "claim": "FirstPlan v1 can structurally represent incomplete exposure, with exposure_complete=false and bounds LOWER_BOUND or UNKNOWN. UNKNOWN requires null credited_sets; EXACT rejects unknown_role_sets. LOWER_BOUND currently has no strong extra model invariant: do not treat mere DTO acceptance as scientifically validated accounting. READY additionally requires exposure_complete=true, which requires all 15 EXACT zones.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_contracts/blueprint_first_plan_v1.py:391-439",
        "tools/science_contracts/blueprint_first_plan_v1.py:675-709",
        "docs/science/sci-p01-p02/CONTRACT.md:85-103"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "claim": "validate_exchange validates fingerprint, versioned references, input assessment, policy authority/status precedence, canonical identity/context, exclusions, cadence, time, prescribed totals and READY. It does not recompute all source muscle roles/credits: this remains producer responsibility. A new overlay must not exploit this responsibility boundary to claim false exact exposure.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_contracts/blueprint_first_plan_v1.py:493-554",
        "tools/science_contracts/blueprint_first_plan_v1.py:618-733",
        "docs/science/sci-p01-p02/CONTRACT.md:91-103"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "claim": "Producer1.0.0 always emits candidate_plan=null and POLICY_UNAVAILABLE unless required input precedence changes status; registry approved_policy_refs is empty. Source/policy hashes are pinned. New science artefact cannot make this producer READY or silently update its source snapshots.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_initial_policy/producer.py:17-26",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/producer.py:71-98",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/registry.py:38-80"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "claim": "Coverage matrix distinguishes DIRECT, INDIRECT_KNOWN, MINOR_KNOWN, UNKNOWN, NONE_KNOWN; NONE_KNOWN means no listed role rather than zero physiology. Admissible counts are based on old eligible dispositions. Do not drop UNKNOWN or compute a false completeness score from absence.",
      "refs": [
        "tools/science_initial_policy/curation_fixtures.py:12-47",
        "tools/science_initial_policy/curation_fixtures.py:71-95",
        "tests/test_science_candidate_curation.py:258-273"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "claim": "Legacy slot/coverage/product modules use 11-zone body_zone_source and exercise_properties taxonomy, rather than SCI 15-zone catalogue. SlotIntent identifies programming target, not exact recruitment. Legacy set-contribution-v1 gives unclassified/no-role no credit, whereas SCI UNKNOWN remains explicitly unknown. Do not transfer this older accounting convention into SCI.",
      "refs": [
        "app/services/slot_intent.py:198-214",
        "app/services/morpho_program_generator.py:169-202",
        "app/services/set_contribution.py:14-27",
        "app/services/set_contribution.py:132-147",
        "app/services/zone_exposure.py:22-32",
        "tests/test_sci_exposure.py:259-286"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F10",
      "claim": "SCI credit coefficients PRIMARY1/SECONDARY0.5/MINOR0/UNKNOWN sentinel are accounting policy, not per-muscle physiology, hypertrophic percentages or a valid mapping from acute EMG. E0 EV-08/09/10 distinguishes measured comparison and conventional mapping; EV-70/71 forbids EMG-only PRIMARY and specifies role authority. No coefficient change is needed for an epistemic annotation.",
      "refs": [
        "data/sci/exposure_credit_policy.json:1-12",
        "data/sci/evidence_registry.json:30-40",
        "data/sci/evidence_registry.json:266-272",
        "app/services/sci_catalogue.py:137-167",
        "docs/strategy/Sx_SCI_V2_CATALOGUE_INTEGRATION_01_SPEC.md:203-228"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F11",
      "claim": "Mobile FirstPlanClient has no default producer/endpoint and fails NOT_SERVED by default. It checks pinned structural schemas and fingerprint/engine then delegates scientific validity to trusted producer.verify(validate_exchange). Its READY guard alone checks approved request/reviewed plan, not all 15 exact bounds; schema alone cannot certify the semantics. Future v2 integration must preserve this trusted verification and fail closed on unsupported versions/keywords.",
      "refs": [
        "clients/mobile/src/api/firstPlan.ts:1-20",
        "clients/mobile/src/api/firstPlan.ts:28-58",
        "clients/mobile/src/api/scienceSchema.ts:1-24",
        "clients/mobile/src/api/firstPlan.test.ts:75-95"
      ]
    }
